From: Denton Gentry <denny@geekhold.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:44:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd_cli: Treat UNKNOWN COMMAND as a failure of the STA commands

wpa_ctrl_command_sta() only treats a "FAIL" reply as a failure. Any
other reply becomes the station address for the next STA-NEXT command.
wpa_supplicant without CONFIG_AP replies "UNKNOWN COMMAND" to STA-FIRST
and STA-NEXT, so "hostapd_cli -p /var/run/wpa_supplicant all_sta" (or
list_sta) loops at 100% CPU and sends "STA-NEXT UNKNOWN COMMAND" for
ever:

  recvfrom(3, "UNKNOWN COMMAND\n", 4095, 0, NULL, NULL) = 16
  sendto(3, "STA-NEXT UNKNOWN COMMAND", 24, 0, NULL, 0) = 24

Treat "UNKNOWN COMMAND" as a failure, like wpa_cli already does in its
copy of wpa_ctrl_command_sta().

Signed-off-by: Denton Gentry <denny@geekhold.com>
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/hostapd/hostapd_cli.c
+++ b/hostapd/hostapd_cli.c
@@ -763,7 +763,8 @@ static int wpa_ctrl_command_sta(struct w
 	}
 
 	buf[len] = '\0';
-	if (memcmp(buf, "FAIL", 4) == 0)
+	if (memcmp(buf, "FAIL", 4) == 0 ||
+	    memcmp(buf, "UNKNOWN COMMAND", 15) == 0)
 		return -1;
 	if (print)
 		printf("%s", buf);
